@marla: storm's bad. we've got ~24 CHI routes with heavy exceptions this morning
@gordon: just heard a semi jackknifed on the ramp — that's INC-2025-00417. everyone ok?
@tokafor: driver's fine, unit's not. recovery en route, I'll open the work order
@marla: holding remaining routes. RTE-CHI-20250115-201 is the one that went down
@marcus: Kellerman already called. their freight is in this batch. going to be a credit conversation
@gordon: file the incident report today. let's get ahead of the tickets

@marcus: getting worried about Kellerman (CLI-0042). on-time's been sliding since the Q2 QBR and tickets are up
@elaine: is it a CHI capacity thing or something systemic?
@marcus: bit of both. moving them to watch. going to need a real plan before Q3
@dana: strategic account, let's not let this become a churn story

@marcus: Kellerman (CLI-0042) is officially at-risk. they're evaluating alternatives
@dana: ok this is a retention fire drill. save plan written?
@marcus: yes, CRM-9030. dedicated CHI capacity + weekly scorecard + exec sponsor
@gordon: ops will support the dedicated capacity for peak. let's not lose them

@sandra: getting multiple 'wrong item' tickets out of IND this morning
@alicia: yeah it's a pattern, opening INC-2025-02233. smells like a bin issue
@priya.n: confirmed — bin label doesn't match WMS. several orders pulled from it
@alicia: freeze that bin, scan-to-confirm going forward. postmortem friday

@kellsworth: deactivated DRV-01188 for cause. he's disputing the 08/21 no-show
@frank: dispatch log for that day says he CALLED IN a mechanical and waited for a callback. that contradicts our written warning
@sackerman: that's the problem — HR-9301 says no-call/no-show, DN-900002 says he notified the hub. we need to reconcile before this goes anywhere
@kellsworth: driver agreement LGL-9002 covers termination for cause, but the conflicting record weakens it. let's get the phone logs

@gordon: peak is here. volume's up ~40% network-wide vs baseline, exceptions climbing everywhere
@marla: CHI is slammed, watching the weather too — do NOT want a repeat of January
@alicia: IND holding up post-mispick fix. scan-to-confirm is slowing us slightly but accuracy's good
@frank: fleet's stretched, PMs deferred where safe. flag anything unsafe
@yolanda: overlap risk with the Kellerman save plan — they get dedicated CHI capacity, protect it
